# PRODUCTION — non-secret RUNTIME config (read from process.env by the server).
# Was fly.production.toml [env]. See config/env/README.md and D-85. Genuine
# secrets (Stripe live keys, LIVEKIT_API_SECRET, etc.) stay in Infisical.
#
# NODE_ENV / PORT stay Fly/Docker-native (not here).
#
# Differences from preview, all deliberate:
#   - NO Supabase vars: storage is unconditionally R2 in production.
#   - The gated video flags (LESSON_INSIGHTS_TRANSCRIPTION / LIVE_CAPTIONS /
#     CLASS_RECORDING) were off at first, and are on here as of D-94
#     (2026-07-21) — see D-94 for the record. The per-student D-22
#     insights-consent check in lib/lesson-notes/consent.ts is independent of
#     these flags and is what gates who actually gets voice captured.

# Server-side Sentry/PostHog — SHARED with preview (same as NEXT_PUBLIC twins).
SENTRY_DSN=__LOCAL__
POSTHOG_KEY=__LOCAL__
POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# Production URLs.
APP_URL=https://spiralclass.com
BETTER_AUTH_URL=https://spiralclass.com

# Production email sender. Requires updates.spiralclass.com SPF/DKIM verified
# in Resend (preview uses the updates.staging.spiralclass.com subdomain).
# D-138: moved 2026-08-29, after updates.spiralclass.com verified in Resend
# (us-east-1, `send` return-path, its own DKIM key — the key copied from the old
# zone was that domain's and was replaced). This address delivers the sign-in
# OTP, so it was held on the old domain until Resend actually said Verified.
RESEND_FROM=soporte@updates.spiralclass.com

# Google Sign-In client — SAME client as preview. The paired
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET is in Infisical. REQUIRED:
# https://spiralclass.com/api/auth/callback/google must be an Authorized
# redirect URI on this client in Google Cloud Console, or Sign-In 400s.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=__LOCAL__

# lib/csp.ts: enforce mode on in production.
CSP_ENFORCE=1

# Intro-video AI coach (D-73) — deliberately NOT under the D-21/D-22 legal
# gate (teacher's OWN public intro video, no student data/minors), so it ships
# enabled. Still a no-op until DEEPGRAM_API_KEY (Infisical) + the teacher-videos
# R2 bucket are set on the production app.
INTRO_VIDEO_COACH_ENABLED=1

# AI-generated social-preview images (D-123) — also NOT under the D-21/D-22
# legal gate: a teacher's own marketing image for a share link, no student
# data involved. The upload half of social previews works with this flag off
# (D-123's default is upload-only); this flag turns on the Gemini-generated
# rail specifically. Still a no-op until GEMINI_VERTEX_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY_BASE64
# (Infisical) is also set on the production app — socialPreviewAiEnabled()
# requires both (env.ts).
SOCIAL_PREVIEW_AI_ENABLED=1

# Vertex AI project the Gemini image-generation call runs against (D-127) —
# NOT a secret, same posture as GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID. Shared with preview: it's
# a GCP project id, not an environment-scoped credential.
GEMINI_VERTEX_PROJECT_ID=__LOCAL__

# Stripe subscription Price IDs (UK entity, D-58). Non-secret identifiers; the
# paired STRIPE_SECRET_KEY / STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET / STRIPE_BILLING_WEBHOOK_SECRET
# (live) are in Infisical.
#
# GBP live prices (D-99 fix, 2026-07-27): the original MXN live Prices
# (149/199000/19900 MXN) predated D-99's move of platform billing to GBP —
# code/config said GBP but the live Stripe Price objects were never
# recreated, so checkout was silently still charging MXN. Replaced with 3
# new GBP Prices on prod_ExampleGbpPlans (£7.99/mo, £79.90/yr, £5.99/mo
# founding); the old MXN prices are deactivated (not deleted — Stripe
# retains them for historical invoice/reporting references). Matches
# packages/shared's PLAN_PRICE_MINOR_UNITS_BY_CURRENCY.GBP and preview's
# equivalent test-mode prices in preview.runtime.env.
STRIPE_PRICE_MONTHLY=__LOCAL__
STRIPE_PRICE_ANNUAL=__LOCAL__
STRIPE_PRICE_FOUNDING=__LOCAL__
# The Customer Portal configuration this repo declares
# (apps/web/src/lib/stripe/portal-configuration.ts), applied by
# `pnpm --filter spiralclass-web stripe:portal:sync --apply`. A non-secret id,
# so it lives here beside the Price ids rather than in Infisical.
#
# Created live on 2026-09-01. The account had NO portal configuration at all
# before that, so Stripe marked this one `is_default` and it applies to every
# session already — pinning it here is what makes that explicit rather than
# incidental, and what stops a future Dashboard-created default from quietly
# taking over. Re-running the sync updates this same object in place; it is
# found by its `spiralclass_managed` metadata marker, not by this id.
STRIPE_BILLING_PORTAL_CONFIG_ID=__LOCAL__

# LiveKit (in-class video call). Non-secret halves — the websocket URL is
# already handed to the client in the join grant, and API_KEY is only the
# identifier half. LIVEKIT_API_SECRET (signs tokens) stays in Infisical.
#
# D-94 (2026-07-21): cut production over to the same self-hosted deployment
# preview already uses (docs/deployment/ORACLE_LIVEKIT_PRODUCTION.md), replacing
# LiveKit Cloud. Same RTC_PROVIDER="livekit" — LiveKitProvider talks to any
# LiveKit-API-compatible server, self-hosted or Cloud
# (docs/features/live-calls-video.md) — so this is
# purely a config change, zero app code. Both environments now share ONE
# physical box (same URL/API_KEY as preview), which is a deliberate,
# documented risk acceptance — see D-94 and ORACLE_LIVEKIT_PRODUCTION.md's
# updated "both environments" status section for the capacity ceiling and the
# graduation trigger to a dedicated box.
#
# MANUAL STEP (not done by this commit): update Infisical's production
# LIVEKIT_API_SECRET to match this box's configured secret (the same value
# preview's Infisical entry uses) before deploying — until then production
# mints tokens the box will reject.
#
# Rollback: revert these two lines to the LiveKit Cloud values below (kept as
# a comment) + the matching Infisical secret, redeploy.
#   (LiveKit Cloud, pre-D-94: LIVEKIT_URL=wss://<project>.livekit.cloud, LIVEKIT_API_KEY=<redacted>)
# D-138: moved 2026-08-29 once the Oracle box actually held a certificate for
# livekit.spiralclass.com (Let's Encrypt via tls-alpn-01, expires 2026-11-27).
# Caddy still serves BOTH hostnames, so the old one keeps working for anything
# that has not picked this up.
LIVEKIT_URL=wss://livekit.spiralclass.com
LIVEKIT_API_KEY=__LOCAL__
# Selects the active VideoProvider (docs/features/live-calls-video.md).
# Explicit so a future flip to a second provider is a
# one-line diff here. lib/video/providers/index.ts
RTC_PROVIDER=livekit

# ── D-94 (2026-07-21) turned four gated flags on here. D-114 (2026-08-08)
# turned TWO of them back off ahead of the first promotion. D-131 (2026-08-26)
# turns those two back ON. The control that actually decides whose voice is
# captured is unchanged: the recorded per-pairing consent (D-22),
# guardian-only for a minor.
#
# ON (D-131):
#   LESSON_INSIGHTS_TRANSCRIPTION_ENABLED — per-speaker lesson audio is
#     captured to R2, transcribed, and deleted again unless the teacher opted
#     into retention (lib/transcription/pipeline.ts's derive-then-discard).
#     THIS flag, not the recording one, is what gates capture (D-114,
#     call-recording.ts's maybeStartLessonAudioCapture). It is inert without
#     DEEPGRAM_API_KEY in Infisical (lib/transcription/config.ts), and the
#     focus areas it feeds also need ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.
#   CLASS_RECORDING_ENABLED — the teacher's Record control is shown on web and
#     mobile and the server will start a room-composite recording
#     (lib/video/recording.ts). It also needs LIVEKIT_EGRESS_S3_* (Tofu-owned,
#     not in this file — see preview.runtime.env's header for why grepping the
#     repo for it is misleading).
# Both are OFF at the code level, so the rollback is deleting these two lines
# and redeploying. Turning either back off means restoring the "switched off"
# sentences in packages/shared/src/legal/privacy-policy.ts in the same change.
LESSON_INSIGHTS_TRANSCRIPTION_ENABLED=1
CLASS_RECORDING_ENABLED=1
#
# STILL ON — untouched by D-114. Captions are ephemeral (streamed from the
# room into the captions Agent, translated, published back into the room;
# nothing is stored), which is why they are not part of the same rollback.
# LIVE_CAPTIONS_ENABLED additionally needs DEEPGRAM_API_KEY + ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
# present in production Infisical (verify with `fly secrets list --app
# agendaprofe`, don't assume) or the caption toggle stays hidden despite the
# flag. lib/captions/config.ts
LIVE_CAPTIONS_ENABLED=1
